// Companion to the VSCode_macOS / VSCode_Win keyboard layers (PLAN.md
// §Apps layers). Defaults-first: this file exists ONLY for the chords VS
// Code and the Claude extension ship with no default, so the layer's H J K L
// panel-focus quad and the terminal-profile picker actually do something.
// Everything else on those layers (U/I/O/;/T/G/S/A/C/R and the RAlt tap) rides
// a real existing default and needs nothing added here.
//
// Install: Cmd/Ctrl+Shift+P -> "Preferences: Open Keyboard Shortcuts (JSON)"
// -> merge these entries into the array that opens.
[
  // ---- Panel focus quad (H J K L) — no VS Code default exists for any of
  // these, confirmed against the built-in command IDs directly. Same chords
  // on both OSes, so one set of entries covers VSCode_macOS and VSCode_Win.
  { "key": "ctrl+shift+f13", "command": "workbench.action.navigateLeft" },
  { "key": "ctrl+shift+f14", "command": "workbench.action.navigateDown" },
  { "key": "ctrl+shift+f15", "command": "workbench.action.navigateUp" },
  { "key": "ctrl+shift+f16", "command": "workbench.action.navigateRight" },

  // ---- Terminal profile picker (B). No args -> opens the profile quick
  // pick rather than a fixed shell; verify that's still true on your VS
  // Code version before relying on it.
  { "key": "shift+f19", "command": "workbench.action.terminal.newWithProfile" },

  // ---- Move-tab-to-pane quad + maximize toggle (left hand, row1 + row2
  // outer) — the movement half of the focus/movement split (PLAN.md §WM
  // redesign v2.1); the H/J/K/L quad above is the focus half. All five
  // command IDs confirmed against the VS Code source directly (none have
  // a factory default keybinding, so nothing to collide with). Same
  // chords on both OSes — these commands are cross-platform.
  { "key": "alt+shift+f13", "command": "workbench.action.moveEditorToLeftGroup" },
  { "key": "alt+shift+f14", "command": "workbench.action.moveEditorToBelowGroup" },
  { "key": "alt+shift+f15", "command": "workbench.action.moveEditorToAboveGroup" },
  { "key": "alt+shift+f16", "command": "workbench.action.moveEditorToRightGroup" },
  { "key": "alt+shift+f17", "command": "workbench.action.toggleMaximizeEditorGroup" },
  // Moved 2026-08-25 to row2-left (A/S/D/F) — a true physical mirror of the
  // H/J/K/L focus quad above, which the first placement (row1) wasn't. The
  // chords above are unchanged; only which physical key sends them moved,
  // so nothing here needed editing — noted in case the row1 position ever
  // shows up in an old note and looks like it should still work.

  // ---- Quick-switch between recently used editors (O key), replaced
  // 2026-08-25. `quickOpenPreviousRecentlyUsedEditor` (VS Code's own
  // Ctrl+Tab default) needs Ctrl held continuously while Tab is tapped
  // repeatedly, then released to commit — works fine on a real keyboard,
  // but this key only ever sends one synthetic Ctrl+Tab press per physical
  // tap, so "holding" relies on the OS's keyboard-repeat-rate re-firing Tab
  // while Ctrl stays down. That repeat rate is a system-wide typing-speed
  // setting, not tunable per-binding, and was too fast to pick a specific
  // editor reliably. `showAllEditorsByMostRecentlyUsed` shows the same
  // list as a normal persistent Quick Pick instead — press once, then
  // arrow keys or type-to-filter at your own pace, Enter to confirm. The
  // unbind (`-`) removes VS Code's own Ctrl+Tab default so only one
  // handler answers the key; without it both could fire.
  { "key": "ctrl+tab", "command": "-workbench.action.quickOpenPreviousRecentlyUsedEditor" },
  { "key": "ctrl+tab", "command": "workbench.action.showAllEditorsByMostRecentlyUsed" },

  // ---- Claude extension, Windows only (C key, V key, and the RAlt-tap
  // action) — NOT VERIFIED. The mac chords (Cmd+Shift+Esc for new session,
  // Cmd+Esc for focus/blur) are believed to be the extension's own
  // defaults, which is why they need nothing here. Ctrl+Shift+Esc is
  // Windows' Task Manager, so the layer sends Shift+F18 (new session) /
  // Shift+F17 (focus/blur) on the Windows base instead — but the
  // extension's actual Windows-side command IDs weren't confirmed from
  // outside VS Code. Before flashing, open Ctrl+K Ctrl+S, search "Claude",
  // find "new session" and "focus/toggle" (names may differ), copy their
  // real command IDs in here, and delete this comment block.
  //
  // V (position 40, added 2026-08-25) sends the SAME Shift+F17 as the
  // RAlt-tap shortcut on the Windows base layer — a second, deliberate
  // route to the identical action, reachable once you're already holding
  // RAlt into this layer rather than relying on a quick tap's timing.
  // { "key": "shift+f18", "command": "<claude-extension.newSession — verify>" },
  // { "key": "shift+f17", "command": "<claude-extension.focusToggle — verify>" }
]
